{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1329,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: Today I’ve got guest and Physicist\nMax Tegmark here to answer some questions…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4899,
    "dDurationMs": 3011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, Max, why should I care about nuclear weapons?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7910,
    "dDurationMs": 3609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Max: Because we’ve learned that they’re\neven more dangerous than we first thought:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11519,
    "dDurationMs": 4211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The biggest threat from nukes isn’t explosions\nthat each kill millions of people, or radioactive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15730,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fallout that kills even more, or even a high-altitude\nelectromagnetic pulse that causes mayhem by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20800,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frying the electrical grid and electronics\nacross a continent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24050,
    "dDurationMs": 4639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, the biggest threat from nuclear weapons\nis a global nuclear-induced winter, in which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28689,
    "dDurationMs": 4501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fires and smoke from as few as a thousand\nnukes could darken the atmosphere enough to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33190,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plunge Earth into a planet-wide mini ice age\nwith year-round winter-like conditions. This"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38330,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could cause a complete collapse of the global\nfood system and apocalyptic unrest, potentially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43870,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "killing most of us 7 billion people on Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46100,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: But didn’t we get rid of most nuclear\nweapons when the cold war ended?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49290,
    "dDurationMs": 4979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Max: Well… Yes and no. When the cold war\nended, the US and Russia slashed their nuclear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54269,
    "dDurationMs": 4451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arsenals, but they still have about 7000 nukes\neach, which could allow either country to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58720,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "create a nuclear winter all on its own, even\nif the other doesn’t retaliate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62260,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: But why should I worry about nuclear\nwinter when nobody in their right mind would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66400,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ever start a nuclear war?\nMax: Unfortunately, an all-out nuclear assault"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70140,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn’t as unlikely as you might think, because\nthe most likely way for nuclear war to start"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn’t political – it’s accidental. For\nexample, the time faulty computer chips in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78800,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "US alarm systems erroneously signaled incoming\nSoviet missiles and the US started to prepare"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83020,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for full-blown retaliation. Or the time that\nRussian satellites mistook an unusual glint"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87570,
    "dDurationMs": 5510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of sunlight off of clouds for incoming American\nmissiles and an officer averted retaliation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93080,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by ignoring the alarm on gut instinct. Or\nthe time after the cold war ended when Russian"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98140,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "radar systems thought a Norwegian scientific\nrocket was an American nuclear missile and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101920,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "almost launched their missiles in retaliation.\nThese close-calls keep happening, and sooner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107420,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or later our luck is gonna run out and an\nentire nuclear arsenal will be launched accidentally."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111920,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: But isn’t getting rid of nukes a\nnational security threat?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115300,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Max: Well, it’s pretty clear that a country\nonly needs a small number of nuclear weapons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120140,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to effectively deter nuclear attacks, and\nany more are as much a national security threat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125640,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the nation that owns them as to the rest\nof the planet. So given the risks of accidental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130170,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nuclear war and nuclear winter, it’s stupid,\ndangerous, and irresponsible for *any* country"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134890,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on earth to have more nuclear weapons than\nit needs for deterrence. If we just continue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138660,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hoarding excessive nuclear arsenals, winter\nis coming."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142480,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: OK, Max, one more question: why should\nI spend my time worrying about nukes when"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148000,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there’s nothing I can do about them?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149360,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Max: Actually, there *is* something you can\ndo! The nuclear arms race isn’t driven entirely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153470,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by security interests: money drives it too,\nand politicians who like to act tough. In"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158060,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a time when they really should be downgrading,\nthe US \u0026 Russian governments are both planning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to upgrade their arsenals at a huge cost.\nAnd who does that money go to? Well, about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167680,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2% of S\u0026P 500 companies are involved in nuclear\nweapons production, and while you can’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172550,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stop paying taxes, you can help stigmatize\nthe nuclear arms race by divesting from companies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177500,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that produce nuclear weapons. It’s really\neasy, and I’ll give you a link that you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179890,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can put in the video description to a site\nthat helps you do just that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182750,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: Thanks, Max and thanks to the Future\nof Life Institute for their support and help"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186340,
    "dDurationMs": 1269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "producing this video!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
